<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Learners at a school in Kitui each travel to school in one way only. A learner is chosen at random. The table shows the probabilities. The probability for bicycle is missing.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Way of travelling</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Walk</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Matatu</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Boda boda</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Bicycle</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Probability</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.17}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.28}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><nbsp/></cell></row></tabular><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find <m>P(\text{bicycle})</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>P(\text{walks or travels by boda boda})</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find <m>P(\text{does not travel by matatu})</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Each learner travels in exactly one way, so the four ways are mutually exclusive and their probabilities add to 1.</p><p>(a) <m>P(\text{bicycle}) = 1 - ({0.17} + {0.3} + {0.28}) = {0.25}</m>.</p><p>(b) A learner cannot both walk and take a boda boda, so add: <m>{0.17} + {0.28} = {0.45}</m>.</p><p>(c) The complement: <m>P(\text{not matatu}) = 1 - {0.3} = {0.7}</m>. As a check, walk, boda boda and bicycle together give <m>{0.17} + {0.28} + {0.25} = {0.7}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{4}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{9}{20}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{7}{10}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>